<h2>Before the next storm</h2>
<p>A little preparation makes a Groves claim easier to document and harder to dispute. Take dated photos and video of your roof, siding, windows, fences, and each room before hurricane season begins. Pull out all three declarations pages and note each deductible, especially any percentage-based named-storm deductible. Confirm your flood policy is active, since NFIP coverage usually has a 30-day waiting period. Store copies of your policies somewhere you can reach from a phone, and keep the <a href="/weather/">live weather page</a> handy for official NWS alerts when a system is in the Gulf.</p>

